> > and give you a higher (ie worse) score if you get them up there.
>
> I'm curious; what do you mean by this? Why is a higher score worse?

The difference between burdened/dead and unburdened/ascended is
far larger than the difference of a few thousand points once ascended.

Once you leave level 1 there isn't any further opportunity to pick up
items for points.  Both lack of items on the levels and the presense
of opponents strong enough to avoid fighting.  You're in too much of
a hurry to get to the altar.

So it is crucial to be unburdened when you step on that staircase
going up.  And as you move from level it makes sense to drop those
items you only needed on that specific level.  Wands of digging have
very little value on later planes and so on.

Gold has little value per weight so you won't want any.  Gems have
better so you might want some.  Artifacts versus gems by price to
weight ratio is the consideration to make if you want score.



